# Automation source ownership and retirement evidence

Observed 2026-10-15 during autonomous closeout, after main
`9327a3a13f0641f2a8c1897aec0c088be016743a`.
This is an operational observation, not authorization to retire a job.
The [source ledger](issue-986-preservation.json) records every full source SHA,
commit-account identity and remaining external action.

All eight retained F tips still match their original captured identities.
GitHub's commit API maps both author and committer to repository account
`1337isnot1337` for all eight. This establishes account provenance; it does
not identify a particular hosted job or its current scheduler operator.

