The seven finite sources have their mathematical successor in the
[angular/contact-debt consolidation](../reports/target_c_pentagon_activation_and_contact_debt_preservation_2026-10-15.md).
Preserving that content supplies no scheduler-retirement evidence.

On both reached hosts, `homelab` and `Asus`, the same-user process cwd and open
file scan found no research use, and the user unit-file inventory had no E99,
Erdos or swarm unit. Homelab's available crontab had no matching entry; Asus
had no `crontab` executable. These are bounded observations, not proof that no
remote or hosted scheduler exists. The branch-specific GitHub Actions API
reported zero runs for each of the eight branches. GitHub Actions history is
not a hosted Codex or ChatGPT scheduler inventory.

The known Macbook SSH endpoint timed out. A bounded current Codex app-server
thread query exposed only this closeout as active, but its older-thread list
was truncated and it does not enumerate hosted controller ownership or job
retirement. No general hosted scheduler retirement interface was exposed by
the available tools at this inspection.

Two targeted plugin-catalog searches, for Codex scheduled automations and
ChatGPT Tasks, found no suitable scheduler ownership/retirement connector.
The catalog results are not exhaustive; no unrelated plugin was connected.

The exact external decision record needed before deletion is: job/controller
identifier, responsible owner, current enabled/disabled state, branch use and
an explicit retirement or successor record. Until those facts are available,
these refs remain protected. The inaccessible decision does not block source
preservation, PR repairs, worktree review or final verification elsewhere.
